   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ הַזּוֹרֵק מִקְצָת דָּם בַּחוּץ –",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «One who sprinkles part of» the «blood» of an offering, e.g., one sprinkling instead of four, «outside» the Temple courtyard"
  },
  {
   "id": "zevachim.110b.1",
   "daf": "110b",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "חַיָּיב. רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר אוֹמֵר: אַף הַמְנַסֵּךְ מֵי הֶחָג בֶּחָג בַּחוּץ – חַיָּיב. רַבִּי נְחֶמְיָה אוֹמֵר: שְׁיָרֵי הַדָּם (שֶׁהִקְרִיבוּ) [שֶׁהִקְרִיבָן] בַּחוּץ – חַיָּיב.",
   "en": "is «liable. Rabbi Elazar says: So too, one who pours as a libation water» consecrated for the libation «of the festival» of Sukkot, «during the Festival, outside» the courtyard, is «liable. Rabbi Neḥemya says:» For the «remainder of the blood» of an offering that was supposed to be poured at the base of the altar and «that» instead «one sacrificed outside» the courtyard, one is «liable.»"
  }
